  "text": "Dubh is a figure tied to a place. Dublin carries her story in its name. The old form Dubh-linn means the pool of Dub. A deep pool opened in the mouth of the River Liffey. Dubh means dark, so the name reads as dark pool. A slingshot killed her near that water. She had drowned a woman her husband consorted with. The killing became a tangle of betrayal and revenge. The pool sat where fresh water met the sea. Dubh’s fate fused water, revenge, and a city.",
